":"0.41 ± 0.03","numeric":0.41}},{"Measurement_ID":"MCTM-042221","Abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"Cell_line":"MEFs Bax-Bak-DKO","Time(h)":48,"IC50_Dark(M*10^-6)":"1.88 ± 0.30","IC50_Dark_value":1.88,"Method":"MTT","DOI":"10.1002/chem.202201259","Year":2022,"Counterion":"O=[N+]([O-])[O-]","Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-042221","value":"0.92 ± 0.02","numeric":0.92}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":2,"value":0.539,"value_relation":"=","std":0,"type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","temperature_C":37,"doi":"10.1002/chem.202201259","year":2022,"counterion":"O=[N+]([O-])[O-]","record_id":"MLDB-003746","detection":"UV-Vis","method_description":"The log P values for compounds (L1, 1 and 2) were determined by using the shake-flask method and UU-Vis spectrometer. The 1-octanol used in this experiment was pre-saturated with de-ionized water by overnight incubation with shaking a biphasic mixture of the two at room temperature. A 4 mL solution of the compound (ca. 50 μM) was prepared in pre-saturated octanol and 2 mL was used to record UV-Vis spectrum (250-900nm). The remaining 2 mL solution was incubated with 2 mL water in a 5 mL tube. The tube was covered with aluminium foil and vigorously shaken for 2 h using an automated shaker at 37 °C. The tube was then allowed to stand for 15 min and two layers were separated carefully. The octanol layer was used to record UV-Vis spectrum (250 to 900 nm). The log P values were determined using the following formula: Log P = Log(Absorption at 2 h in octanol / (Absorption at 0 h in octanol - Absorption at 2 h in octanol)). The log P value of cisplatin was measured following a similar procedure except for platinum concentration in aqueous and octanol layer was quantified using ICP-MS. All the experiments were carried out in triplicate."}],"ccdc":["ZATCUW"]}